# README Onboarding (Yum4Less)

Follow **`.cursor/rules/yum4less-product-and-trust.mdc`** for doc owners.

## README owns

- What Yum4Less is and **honest beta v1 scope**
- Quick start, prerequisites, commands, env pointers (detail in `.env.example`)
- Trust/security defaults and troubleshooting
- Links to **`PROJECT_CONTINUITY.md`** (history/snapshot) and **`AGENTS.md`** (agents/MCP)

## README does not own

- Changelog, roadmap, competitive analysis, or verification tables → **`PROJECT_CONTINUITY.md`**
- Agent/MCP setup walkthrough detail → **`AGENTS.md`**
- Distilled locked decisions → **`.private/owner-decisions.md`**

## When to update README

- Setup steps, commands, or env vars change
- Public beta scope or onboarding flow changes materially
- Security/deploy defaults change

After material slices, update **`PROJECT_CONTINUITY.md`** per **`yum4less-continuity-journal.mdc`** — do not mirror every slice in README.

Keep README concise and truthful: no investor pitch sections, no file inventories, no duplicate status blocks from continuity.
